<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet xml:id="diaMuertos-ws-tris">
  <title>Tri's</title>

  <introduction>
    
    <p>Three different músicos form a <alert>TRI</alert> (or <alert>SET</alert>, or <alert>BAND</alert>) if, for each aspect, the músicos are either all the same or all different.<fn>This activity is based on the game <url href="https://www.playmonster.com/brands/set/" visual="playmonster.com">SET</url>, and is adapted from <url href="https://jrmf.org/puzzle/monster-town/" visual="jrmf.org">Monster Town</url> by the Julia Robinson Mathematics Festival, used under <url href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" visual="creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</url>.</fn></p>

    <p>For example:</p>

    <image source="diaMuertos-tri.png" width="95%" margins="5% 0%">
      <shortdescription></shortdescription>
    </image>

    <p>
      <tabular top="minor" left="minor" right="minor" bottom="minor" row-headers="yes">
      <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
        <cell></cell><cell>Músico 1</cell><cell>Músico 2</cell><cell>Músico 3</cell><cell>Check</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Face</cell><cell>HUMAN</cell><cell>HUMAN</cell><cell>HUMAN</cell><cell>All the Same</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Body</cell><cell>Dress</cell><cell>Dress</cell><cell>Dress</cell><cell>All the same</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Gift</cell><cell>bread</cell><cell>chocolate</cell><cell>dalia</cell><cell>All Different</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell># of Jaranas</cell><cell>2</cell><cell>0</cell><cell>1</cell><cell>All Different</cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
  </p>
  </introduction>

  <exercise xml:id="ex-tris-which-are-tri">
    <title>Which are a TRI? Why?</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>You can use the tables to check each aspect!</p>
    </introduction>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <title>The Bread Friends</title>
        <sidebyside widths="62% 33%" margins="0% 0%" valign="middle">
          <tabular top="minor" left="minor" right="minor" bottom="minor" row-headers="yes">
            <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
              <cell></cell><cell>Músico 1</cell><cell>Músico 2</cell><cell>Músico 3</cell><cell>Check</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Face</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Body</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Gift</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Jarana</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
          <image source="diaMuertos-breadFriends.png" width="60%">
            <shortdescription>Three músicos titled "Bread Friends", each with a calavera cat face and each holding a loaf of bread as their gift. Left to right — Músico 1: charro suit, holding two jaranas; Músico 2: skeleton body, holding one jarana; Músico 3: black dress with a red bow, holding no jarana.</shortdescription>
          </image>
        </sidebyside>
      </li>
      <li>
        <title>The Choco-Dos</title>
        <sidebyside widths="62% 33%" margins="0% 0%" valign="middle">
          <tabular top="minor" left="minor" right="minor" bottom="minor">
            <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
              <cell></cell><cell>Músico 1</cell><cell>Músico 2</cell><cell>Músico 3</cell><cell>Check</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Face</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Body</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Gift</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Jarana</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
          <image source="diaMuertos-chocoDos.png" width="60%">
            <shortdescription>Three músicos titled "The Choco-Dos". Left to right — Músico 1: white skull face, skeleton body, brings chocolate, holding one jarana; Músico 2: orange fox face with a colorful headdress, charro suit, brings bread (no chocolate), holding no jarana; Músico 3: red calavera cat face, dress, brings chocolate, holding one jarana.</shortdescription>
          </image>
        </sidebyside>
      </li>

    </ol>
  </exercise>

  <exercise xml:id="ex-tris-challenge">
    <title>Challenge</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>Pick the first two músicos independently or at random (for example, work with a partner, and each secretly picks a músico). Fill out the table, and leave the third row blank.</p>
    <p>
      <tabular top="minor" left="minor" right="minor" bottom="minor" row-headers="yes">
      <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
        <cell></cell><cell>Músico 1</cell><cell>Músico 2</cell><cell>Músico 3</cell><cell>Check</cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Face</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Body</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell>Gift</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
      </row>
      <row>
        <cell># of Jaranas</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell>
      </row>
    </tabular>
  </p>

    </introduction>

    <task>
      <p>Is it possible to complete the table to form a TRI? Try!</p>
    </task>

    <task workspace="3cm">
      <p>If you succeeded in forming a TRI, do you think that there was only one way to complete the table with the third músico? Why or why not?</p>
    </task>

    <task workspace="4cm">
      <p>In general, if we pick any two músicos, what can we say about whether it's possible to complete the table to form a TRI, and if the choice is unique? Explain.</p>
    </task>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
